    "release_notes": "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/feature/lorwyn-eclipsed-release-notes",
    "interpretation": "Adds one independent trigger per applicable provider, with fresh IDs, separate modes/targets and complete event context; never exponential and never a stack copy. Trigger-time provider/source facts survive departure. Once-per-turn trigger limits remain binding. Delayed and reflexive abilities are excluded. Intrinsic token end-step sacrifice abilities participate. Triggered mana occurrences use the shared actual/speculative characteristic world and resolve without stack packets."
  },
  "oracle_corrections": [
    "The complete Oracle text refers to another controlled Elemental, including Kindred noncreatures; XMage uses a narrower creature-only filter, which this definition deliberately does not adopt."
  ],
  "test_scope_notes": [
    "The triggered-mana multiplier fixture uses an explicit typed Elemental overlay on Growth to isolate the shared event/funding boundary; ordinary Growth does not have an Elemental subtype. A separate ordinary Growth regression verifies two-mana funding without that overlay."
  ]
